{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bc0b644c18bfb7de","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The output is just `'text-lg'` — not even `'text-lg font-bold'`. It seems like `font-bold` is being stripped too. Let me think about why...\n\n`clsx('text-base', { 'text-lg': true, 'font-bold': false })` would produce `'text-base text-lg'` because `font-bold: false` is filtered out by clsx. So the input to `twMerge` is `'text-base text-lg'`, which collapses to `'text-lg'`.\n\nThe `font-bold` doesn't appear because clsx already filters it out before twMerge sees it!\n\n\nSo I need to test with a non-conflicting class instead of one that twMerge would deduplicate — something like `bg-red-500` would let me verify that twMerge properly merges different classes.\n","signature":"f40664e7c25f4a4ebe78de9fb49e957f"}],"model":"qwen3.6-35b","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":198762,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fb51005-a686-498d-8403-19206d765de7","uuid":"78b22d2b-abe8-4bbc-9134-acaed1dc25c8","timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:53:54.390Z"}
